From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] boringssl: recognise ppc64 as a 64-bit target

base.h dispatches on architecture to define OPENSSL_64_BIT or OPENSSL_32_BIT
over a flat list: x86_64, x86, aarch64, arm, mips, mips64, riscv64, riscv32,
pnacl, wasm, asmjs. powerpc is absent, so on ppc64le nothing matches and
*neither* word-size macro is defined.

crypto_word_t is declared only under those macros:

    #if defined(OPENSSL_64_BIT)
    typedef uint64_t crypto_word_t;
    #elif defined(OPENSSL_32_BIT)
    typedef uint32_t crypto_word_t;

so it gets no definition at all, and every translation unit touching a BIGNUM
or a constant-time helper fails -- "unknown type name 'crypto_word_t'",
"implicit declaration of bn_rshift_words", "implicit declaration of
constant_time_select_w", and onward through crypto/, fipsmodule/ and the GCM
modes.

Declare only the word size. An OPENSSL_PPC64LE would opt into per-architecture
assembly BoringSSL does not carry here, so this takes the generic C path
exactly as the asm-less targets above it do. boring-sys2 already ships
boringssl-loongarch.patch doing the same for LoongArch.

Generated with diff(1) against the pristine crate, not written by hand: the
first version of this patch carried a hunk header of @@ -108,6 +108,9 @@ for a
body of three context lines and three additions, which GNU patch accepted
against an already-modified working copy and rejected against a clean one.

--- a/deps/boringssl/src/include/openssl/base.h
+++ b/deps/boringssl/src/include/openssl/base.h
@@ -107,6 +107,13 @@
 #define OPENSSL_RISCV64
 #elif defined(__riscv) && __SIZEOF_POINTER__ == 4
 #define OPENSSL_32_BIT
+#elif defined(__powerpc64__) || defined(__PPC64__)
+// ppc64, both endiannesses. Only the word size is declared: an OPENSSL_PPC64LE
+// would opt into per-arch assembly BoringSSL does not carry, so this takes the
+// generic C path like the other asm-less targets above. Without it nothing
+// matches, neither OPENSSL_64_BIT nor OPENSSL_32_BIT is defined, and
+// crypto_word_t has no definition -- which is every error in the first build.
+#define OPENSSL_64_BIT
 #elif defined(__pnacl__)
 #define OPENSSL_32_BIT
 #define OPENSSL_PNACL
